From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:18:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Tie the data to the account, and show health instead of
 risk
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Six changes, one of which was a data leak.

Signing out only cleared the email address. The profile, the payments,
the alerts all stayed on the phone, so the next person to sign in was
shown someone else's money under their own name — and it looked like it
was working, which is what made it dangerous. Sign-out now clears the
phone, sign-in downloads that account's own data before handing the app
over, and backup runs automatically a few seconds after each change
rather than waiting for a button nobody presses.

While in there: sanitizePersistedState was silently dropping the session
token and the dismissed-alert list on every load, so "remember this
device" was saved correctly and then thrown away on the way back in.

The gauge showed raw risk, so somebody in perfect shape saw a white
"0 / 100" above an empty bar. It shows health now — risk turned inside
out at the last moment before pixels, green sliding to red as it falls.
The engine still speaks in risk, so no threshold or test moved.

Confirming an email had a "Continue to the app" button under it, which
meant nobody ever confirmed anything. It is a screen of its own now and
it waits, polling every four seconds and immediately on foreground, so
tapping the link in a mail app advances it before you look back. Brevo
accepts a send and rejects it afterwards, so a quiet way past appears
after two minutes — otherwise a rejected sender strands everyone.

Also: a 60-second countdown on both resend buttons, matching the
server's own limit, and a forgotten-password flow — in-app request, a
one-use link that expires in an hour, a web form for the new password,
and every device signed out once it is used.

